# Public HTTPS URL of a Midnight proof server.
#
# Leave unset for the default demo behaviour: circuits run unproven in memory.
# Proving keys are served from public/ either way -- keys are an input to a
# prover, and the prover is the proof server, so keys alone change nothing.
#
# In the devcontainer, start the proof server and expose it:
#   docker compose -f proof-server/docker-compose.yml up -d
#   .devcontainer/tunnel.sh
# then copy the printed URL here (as ui/.env.local, which is gitignored).
#
# Must be https:// if the page itself is served over https, or the browser
# blocks it as mixed content.
# VITE_PROOF_SERVER_URL=https://example.trycloudflare.com

# ── Live on-chain mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The address printed by `cli/npm run deploy`, also written to
# cli/.deployments/<network>.json. Without it the app has no market to join and
# only the in-memory demo is available.
# VITE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# Must match the network Lace is set to, or the wallet refuses to connect.
# VITE_NETWORK_ID=preview
#
# Note: in live mode the proof server and indexer URLs come from Lace itself
# (getConfiguration), NOT from VITE_PROOF_SERVER_URL above. Each user runs
# their own proof server; this site does not host one.
